{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":24340,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"d160efc629830c63ff9e783729c63ef0cec573f2b96097a1bacc33a44a573433","packTokens":9502,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"side","tokens":100,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":9340,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PRODUCT SIDE. This run builds the API side of the product these requirements describe, in an existing .NET API project: every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there, and the data behind them. The web app is built in its own repo: no screen is built here, and no criterion is written for one.\n\nState, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API in the existing ASP.NET Core .NET 9 project shall implement every method, path, parameter, header, request and response schema, media type, and status defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, without adding uncontracted business operations.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Every operation in the locked contract has a valid authorized request and record fixtures. when A client calls each declared operation using its method, path, parameters, headers, and request media type. then The response status, media type, and body fields match the operation's declared successful response.\",\n    \"Given An operation declares invalid-input, authentication, authorization, not-found, conflict, or server-error responses. when The corresponding condition is sent through that operation. then The response status and error body match a response declared for that operation.\",\n    \"Given A path and method are absent from the locked contract. when A request is sent to that path and method. then The response status is 404 or 405 and no business record is created.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement the locked contract under the `/api` path prefix, expose no uncontracted business operation, and preserve the existing root health response, OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API is running. when A client calls `/`, `/openapi/v1.json`, and `/swagger`. then Each response status is 200, the root response value is `API is up`, and the OpenAPI response includes the contracted `/api` operations.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist records, relationships, state changes, and file artifacts required by contracted operations in the configured shared database, keep successful mutations available after process restart, avoid importing legacy spreadsheet or paper-process business data, and support deployment bootstrap and explicitly enabled demo seed data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid contracted create or update request is made against a configured database. when The request succeeds, the application restarts, and the resource is fetched through its contracted read operation. then The response status is successful and the returned record fields match the persisted row.\",\n    \"Given A contracted upload operation receives a valid evidence or logger file. when The API restarts and the related contracted read or download operation is called. then The response status is successful and the returned file or record fields match the uploaded content and metadata.\",\n    \"Given Legacy spreadsheet or paper-process data exists outside a new configured database and has not been submitted through contracted operations. when The API starts and contracted collections are queried. then The database contains no imported legacy business row and response lists contain no imported legacy records.\",\n    \"Given Deployment bootstrap configuration supplies the initial System Administrator identity, warehouse records, and customer-organisation records. when The API starts against an empty database. then The database contains rows for the configured initial administrator, warehouses, and organisations before contracted operations are served.\",\n    \"Given A deployment supplies demo seed records and `Seed:Demo` is explicitly enabled or disabled. when The API starts against an empty database. then The database contains the configured demo seed rows only when `Seed:Demo` is enabled, and contains no demo seed rows when it is disabled.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall provide contracted staff authorization-URL lookup, customer email-and-password sign-in with one-time-code verification and resend, and password-reset request, token-inspection, and completion flows, deliver customer codes and reset links by email, and enforce configured verification and resend attempt limits.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An active customer account has valid credentials and configured email delivery. when The customer submits credentials to the contracted sign-in operation. then The response contains a challenge identifier, an email message contains the one-time code, and no authenticated customer result is issued before code verification.\",\n    \"Given A customer challenge is pending. when The customer verifies a valid code, submits an invalid or reused code, or requests a resend. then Each response status and returned authentication or challenge value reflects the contract-defined outcome, and only a valid unused code produces an authenticated customer result.\",\n    \"Given A customer account requests a password reset. when The account requests, inspects, and completes a reset using the issued token. then The response values identify token usability, the reset link is sent by email, and a consumed or invalid token cannot reset the password again.\",\n    \"Given The staff identity-provider authorization URL is configured. when An unauthenticated client calls the staff authorization-URL operation. then The response status is 200 and the returned value is the configured URL.\",\n    \"Given A customer submits an unknown email address or an incorrect password. when The customer calls the sign-in operation for each case. then The response status and error body are the same for both cases, and no challenge value or authenticated result is returned.\",\n    \"Given A customer submits an expired or previously used code, attempts sign-in for a deactivated account, or calls the staff authorization-URL operation while its URL is unconfigured. when The corresponding contracted operation is called. then The response status and error body match a declared failure response, and no authenticated result or unusable authorization URL is returned.\",\n    \"Given A customer has exceeded the deployment-configured verification or resend attempt limit. when The customer submits another code verification or resend request. then The response status is a declared failure status and no authenticated result or additional one-time-code email message is issued.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall validate staff identities using the configured Meridian Microsoft identity provider, separately from customer email-and-password authentication, map authenticated staff identities to active persisted accounts, and enforce contracted customer-organisation, staff-role, warehouse-scope, Auditor read-only, and account-status restrictions on every operation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Customer organisations have separate orders, deliveries, certificates, or recall records. when An authenticated user from one organisation lists or requests another organisation's records. then The response status is 403 or the contract-defined not-found status and contains no other-organisation record.\",\n    \"Given A staff member is assigned to one warehouse and another warehouse has records. when The staff member lists or requests warehouse-scoped stock, receipts, orders, routes, or quality records outside the assignment. then The response list contains only assigned-warehouse records and an inaccessible-record response contains no record value.\",\n    \"Given An Auditor is authenticated and a record is available. when The Auditor reads the record and attempts a contracted create, update, or delete operation. then The read response contains the record and each prohibited write response status is 403.\",\n    \"Given An account has been deactivated or removed. when That account makes a subsequent authenticated request to a protected contracted operation. then The response status is 401 or 403 and contains no protected record.\",\n    \"Given A Quality Manager or Auditor is authenticated and requests a record in a warehouse outside an ordinary staff member's assignment. when The account reads that record. then The response status is successful and the returned record belongs to the requested warehouse.\",\n    \"Given A request supplies a valid token issued by the configured Meridian Microsoft identity provider for an active staff account, or supplies an invalid, untrusted, unknown-account, or deactivated-account identity. when The caller invokes a protected contracted staff operation. then The response status and accessible records reflect the matched persisted account's roles and warehouse assignments, and an invalid or inactive identity receives status 401 or 403 with no protected record.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist searchable products and immutable versioned temperature profiles, require a profile for each product, and validate profile tiers and governance history.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A System Administrator creates or searches for a product. when The product is submitted, listed, retrieved, or deactivated through contracted operations. then The response record contains the submitted product specification and active state, and searches return matching product records.\",\n    \"Given A product has no valid temperature profile or a profile has overlapping or discontinuous tier boundaries. when The product or profile is submitted. then The response status is 400 and the response error identifies the invalid profile or tier values.\",\n    \"Given A valid profile change includes an effective date, label, limits, tiers, and reason. when A System Administrator creates the profile version and later lists versions. then The response record and profile list contain the new version, reason, effective date, and actor, while the previous version remains returned unchanged.\",\n    \"Given A product has an earlier profile version. when A caller attempts to alter that earlier version rather than create a new version. then The response status is 409 and the earlier profile record remains unchanged.\",\n    \"Given A product is deactivated. when A customer submits an order line for that product. then The response status is 400 or 409 as declared by the operation and the response does not report a successful order.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist separate contracted receipt, receipt-logger, receipt-evidence, stock, movement, and opening-stock records and enforce receipt traceability, quarantine, expiry validation, and Quality Officer release, while allowing a Quality Officer to release an ordinary eligible receipt without the separate two-person approval required for decisions that invoke that workflow.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A permitted Warehouse Operator submits a valid receipt with product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and location. when The operator creates the receipt and retrieves it. then The response record contains the submitted values and a Quarantined status.\",\n    \"Given A product and lot number already have a receipt. when A second permitted receipt with the same product and lot number is submitted. then The response contains a distinct receipt identifier and the stock list reports both quantities without merging receipt records.\",\n    \"Given A receipt expiry date is before the current date, or release is attempted when expiry is within 30 days of receipt. when The receipt or release action is submitted. then The response status is 400 or 409 as defined by the operation and the receipt or release status value is not changed to Released.\",\n    \"Given A valid supplier-format logger file or separate evidence file is available for an existing receipt. when The file is uploaded through its contracted receipt operation and the receipt is subsequently fetched. then The response contains the receipt record or action result and a subsequent receipt response contains the stored file-related record or processed readings.\",\n    \"Given A handling unit has positive available quantity at a warehouse location. when A permitted move or opening-stock operation is submitted. then The response record contains the resulting quantity and location, and a movement record contains actor, time, source, destination, and moved quantity.\",\n    \"Given A receipt is quarantined, meets the expiry restrictions, and has no condition requiring a two-person quality decision. when An authorized Quality Officer releases the receipt through its contracted workflow. then The response record contains the Quality Officer as the decision actor and the stock status is Released; this receipt release does not bypass a separately required two-person decision.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a handling unit reaches the end of its expiry date in its warehouse's configured local time zone, the Meridian API shall mark it Expired even if it is Quarantined or On Hold, remove it from allocations, apply the contracted replacement-allocation and order-status rules, record the change, and alert the dispatcher.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A handling unit is allocated to an order and its expiry date ends in the warehouse's configured local time zone. when The scheduled expiry check runs at the start of the next local calendar day. then The stock row has Expired status even if it was Quarantined or On Hold, its allocation rows are removed, the order row reflects any replacement allocation, and an audit event and dispatcher alert email call record the change.\",\n    \"Given A released handling unit is allocated to an order and has passed its expiry date in the warehouse's configured local time zone. when The scheduled expiry check runs. then The stock row has Expired status, the allocation count for that unit is zero unless eligible replacement stock is allocated, the affected order status and outstanding quantity reflect the replacement outcome, and a dispatcher alert row identifies the expiry notification.\",\n    \"Given An order contains an allocation that expires and no suitable replacement stock is available. when The scheduled expiry check runs. then A partial order response shows Partly Allocated status and the outstanding quantity, while a complete-only order row has no allocations and Submitted status; the expired stock row has Expired status and a dispatcher alert row records the outcome.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist customer orders and dispatch allocations using the serving warehouse's deployment-configured cut-off, working-day, holiday, time-zone, and customer shelf-life rules, and enforce idempotency, order validation, pre-packing customer changes, and cancellation rules.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated customer submits an order with at least one line, positive pack quantities, an organisation-owned address, and an idempotency key. when The order is submitted twice with the same key and payload. then Both response bodies return the same order identifier and the order list contains one order.\",\n    \"Given A customer submits an invalid line, another organisation's address, a date earlier than permitted, or a product inactive for ordering. when The customer places the order. then The response status is 400 or 409 and no order row is created.\",\n    \"Given The serving warehouse has deployment-supplied cut-off, working-day, holiday, and local time-zone configuration. when A customer requests an order delivery date before or after cut-off. then The response record accepts no date earlier than the next working day before cut-off or the working day after that when submitted after cut-off.\",\n    \"Given An order is not yet Packed or has already reached Packed status. when The customer attempts to change or cancel it. then The response status and order status value reflect the applicable lifecycle rule, and successful cancellation returns the allocated quantity to available stock.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall allocate only released, physically available stock meeting customer minimum remaining shelf life, select earliest expiry first with the specified stability-budget tie-break, and apply complete-order, partial-order, back-order, and override rules.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Released stock is available for an order from its serving warehouse and has eligible lots. when The order is allocated. then The response record shows earliest-expiry eligible lots first, applies minimum remaining shelf life, uses greater stability-budget usage first for tied expiry dates, and exposes each allocation and outstanding quantity.\",\n    \"Given Suitable stock is insufficient for a partial order or any line of a complete-only order. when Allocation is attempted. then The partial order response shows allocated and outstanding quantities without over-allocating stock, while the complete-only order holds no stock until every line can be fully allocated.\",\n    \"Given Multiple orders are submitted concurrently against the same available handling units. when The allocations are committed. then The response records and stock list show no unit allocated to more than one order and total allocated quantity does not exceed physical available quantity.\",\n    \"Given A dispatcher submits an allocation override with a reason, without a reason, or to stock violating Released status or customer shelf life. when The override operation is called. then The valid response record includes the reason and changed allocation, while each invalid response status is 400 or 409 and the original allocation remains unchanged.\",\n    \"Given Suitable stock is released for waiting back orders. when The allocation service updates affected orders. then The order response records show oldest-first back-order allocation.\",\n    \"Given An older back order awaits suitable stock or a complete-only order cannot be fully allocated. when Suitable stock is released or allocation is attempted. then The response record shows eligible back orders filled in submission order and no stock held by the incomplete complete-only order.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist compatible box packing and route plans, enforce box and route qualification, and record driver loading, departure, synchronization, handover, refusal, and delivery-evidence operations.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Warehouse Operator submits a pack request for allocated stock. when The requested box contains one logger, products with the same storage band, and a compatible box type. then The response record contains the box, logger, lot quantities, operator, and seal time; a reused logger or incompatible packing response status is 409.\",\n    \"Given A dispatcher submits a route with date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times. when The route is created, updated, or confirmed. then The response record contains the requested route values and a conflicting driver or vehicle assignment returns status 409.\",\n    \"Given A route's packed box would exceed qualified duration less the configured safety margin at a planned arrival. when The route confirmation operation is called. then The response status is 409 and the response message identifies the box and qualification shortfall or duration overrun.\",\n    \"Given A driver calls route listing, route detail, scan, departure, or synchronization operations for the authenticated driver's route. when The driver supplies contracted date, action identifiers, or route data. then The response list or record contains only that driver's authorized route, ordered stops, expected boxes, scans, and departure state.\",\n    \"Given A driver synchronizes queued actions with distinct action identifiers or repeats an action identifier. when The synchronization operation is called. then The response record contains accepted and conflicting actions, and the resulting route history contains each accepted action only once.\",\n    \"Given A driver submits a handover with receiver, acknowledgement, signature, photo, completion time, and box delivery or refusal quantities. when The handover operation is called and authorized delivery evidence is subsequently fetched. then The response record and delivery-evidence response contain persisted evidence and quantities, and refused quantities retain the refusal reason.\",\n    \"Given A confirmed route is changed before its driver has left for the affected stop. when A dispatcher updates the route schedule or stop order. then The response record contains the changed schedule or stop order and an email call or driver-change event is recorded.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall process readings from contracted receipt logger uploads and from the configured authenticated logger gateway through the locked contract operation, expose temperature histories for contracted entity types, and persist available readings, gaps, excursions, tier-by-tier handling-unit budgets, related holds, and corrected history when readings arrive late or out of order.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A contracted receipt logger upload contains repeated, late, out-of-order, future-dated, or pre-sealing readings. when The file is processed and temperature history is requested for its entity and date range. then The response record places readings at their occurred times, stores a duplicate once, flags future and pre-sealing readings as excluded from calculations, and shows unavailable-reading gaps.\",\n    \"Given Three consecutive in-band readings follow an out-of-band reading in persisted history. when The related temperature history and handling-unit record are requested. then The response records show the excursion open from the first out-of-band reading until the third consecutive in-band reading and show time charged to each applicable tier.\",\n    \"Given A handling unit has excursion history or a late reading changes that history. when The handling-unit or temperature-history operation is called after recalculation. then The response record shows separate budgets for portions with different histories, updated remaining tier allowances, excursion links, holds, and an audit event for the correction.\",\n    \"Given An excursion begins, a tier allowance falls below 25 percent, a tier is exhausted, or a not-permitted range is reached. when The triggering reading is received and processed. then An email call is recorded within 120 seconds for the required driver when on-route, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers, and affected stock response records have On Hold status pending a decision.\",\n    \"Given A logger has sent no reading for 15 minutes and its box is out for delivery. when The silent-device check runs and temperature history is requested. then The response record marks the device silent, shows the gap, and an alert email call is recorded.\",\n    \"Given A cold room or its temperature records are available. when A caller lists cold rooms, retrieves a cold room, or requests temperature history for a room, box, lot, handling unit, or device. then The response list or record contains the latest reading, status, gaps, alerts, history timestamps, and applicable band and excursion markers.\",\n    \"Given A handling unit has recorded temperature history with an interval containing no readings and a stored profile band. when The caller fetches temperature history for the unit or its box, lot, device, or cold room. then The response contains readings in recorded-time order, an explicit gap, and temperature-band and excursion fields for the requested interval.\",\n    \"Given The configured authenticated logger gateway has a batch of readings for known devices, including duplicate, late, or out-of-order readings. when The gateway submits the batch through the locked contract operation using its configured credentials. then The persisted reading rows contain each valid reading once at its occurred time, and contracted temperature-history responses show the same ordered readings and calculated history regardless of batch arrival order.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist quality cases, signed proposals and decisions, superseding decisions, and destruction records, apply the required two-person quality approval, make the latest valid signed disposition authoritative for extant stock, and preserve prior decision history without restoring stock already destroyed or delivered.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Quality Officer submits a disposition proposal subject to the two-person approval workflow, with disposition, reason, and identity confirmation. when The proposal is retrieved or a decision is submitted by the proposing officer or an eligible different Quality Manager. then The response record contains the proposal and actor, the proposing officer cannot approve their own proposal, and a different eligible manager's approval or return is recorded without replacing the proposal; this approval restriction does not apply to an ordinary receipt release under AC-7.6.\",\n    \"Given A quality decision exists for stock that has not been destroyed or delivered, and an authorized caller submits a separately signed superseding decision. when The supersede operation is called and the decision and affected stock are subsequently retrieved. then The response record contains the new current decision and the earlier decision remains in the returned decision history; the stock status reflects the superseding disposition, a change away from Released removes remaining allocations and applies the contracted replacement-allocation rules, and a decision that would change the status of destroyed or delivered quantity returns status 409 with the prior decision and stock status unchanged.\",\n    \"Given Rejected stock has a positive quantity to destroy. when An authorized caller submits a destruction date, quantity, and witness. then The response record contains those values and the destroyed quantity is removed from available stock.\",\n    \"Given A handling unit has tiered budget usage and a related quality case. when An authorized Quality Officer fetches the unit and quality case. then The response contains the used and remaining value for each tier and linked case telemetry and decision fields.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist signed recalls, trace selected lots through affected stock and delivery records, block affected stock still held, and record customer responses and signed closure or write-off decisions until quantities are accounted for.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An eligible Quality Manager starts a signed recall for selected product lots. when The recall is started and its record and trace are requested. then The response records identify affected stock, warehouse locations, boxes, routes, deliveries, customer response progress, and recalled held stock is unavailable for allocation.\",\n    \"Given A customer submits or updates a recall response for an authorized delivery. when The recall response operation is called. then The response record contains on-hand, used, destroyed, and stated-disposition values and recall progress reflects the submitted quantities.\",\n    \"Given A recall has unaccounted quantity or all quantity is accounted for. when A Quality Manager submits closure or a signed write-off. then The response status is 409 for closure with unaccounted quantity and no valid write-off, or the response record contains the signed closure or write-off when preconditions are met.\",\n    \"Given A started recall has affected warehouse, box, route, and delivery records. when Recall-trace and lot-history operations are called. then The response lists contain the chronological trace of the lot through warehouse, boxes, routes, deliveries, movements, and destruction records.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement customer organisation account, address, team, delivery, certificate, recall-notice, order, and language-preference operations with returned records and mutations scoped to the authenticated organisation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An authenticated customer requests orders, deliveries, delivery details, certificates, certificate files, or recall notices. when The corresponding customer operation is called. then The response list, record, or PDF file contains only records belonging to that customer's organisation.\",\n    \"Given A Customer Administrator submits a valid saved address or invitation, changes an address, or removes an address or team member within their organisation. when The contracted customer-administration operation is called. then The response record or action result identifies the change and subsequent lists contain the updated organisation-scoped address or team record.\",\n    \"Given A Customer Administrator attempts to edit or remove an address or member belonging to another organisation. when The contracted customer-administration operation is called. then The response status is 403 or the contract-defined not-found status and no other-organisation row is changed.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated customer account has a saved language preference. when The account is retrieved and patched with `en` or `ar`. then The response record contains the saved language value and a value outside the contract enum returns status 400.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement contracted administration, operational-report, and lot-history operations, persisting organisation shelf-life settings, account role and warehouse assignments, and chronological business records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A System Administrator requests organisations, organization details, accounts, or account details. when The corresponding list or retrieval operation is called. then The response list or record contains persisted organization, member, address, shelf-life, role, and access-assignment values within caller authorization scope.\",\n    \"Given A System Administrator creates, updates, or deactivates an account or updates an organization's minimum remaining shelf life. when The contracted administration operation is called. then The response status and record or action result reflect the new account state, roles, assignments, or minimum shelf-life value.\",\n    \"Given An authorized caller requests an operational report for a permitted date range and warehouse or requests lot history. when The report or lot-history operation is called. then The response record or list contains only authorized report values and chronologically ordered receipt, movement, delivery, and destruction events for the requested lot.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall record the actor and timestamp for consequential contracted changes and decisions in read-only audit events and retain those events without automatic expiry.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A consequential contracted change or decision is successfully recorded. when An authorized caller queries audit events using supported search, date, action-type, or user filters. then The response list contains the event's actor, timestamp, action type, affected record, and applies the supplied filters.\",\n    \"Given An audit event has been recorded. when Time passes and the event is queried again or a write is attempted. then The response list still contains the event and a write attempt against the audit event returns status 403.\",\n    \"Given An authenticated actor performs a consequential contracted mutation or decision. when The operation completes and the authorized audit-events operation is queried for the actor and time range. then The response list and audit row contain the actor, event time, and action type.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall fail startup when persistent-storage configuration is invalid and return the contract-defined server-error response without reporting a business operation as successful when storage is unavailable during a contracted operation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The database configuration is invalid. when The API process starts. then The process exits before serving contracted operations and startup output contains an error.\",\n    \"Given The API is running and its configured database becomes unavailable during a contracted operation. when The operation is called. then The response status is 500 with the contract-defined `server_error` code and no success response or success record is returned.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"Excursion alerts are sent through the configured email channel to the driver when applicable, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers after the triggering reading is received through the contracted authenticated logger-gateway operation.\",\n  \"The contracted authenticated logger-gateway operation and temperature-data processing capability support concurrent readings from logger and cold-room devices.\",\n  \"Consequential-operation audit events contain an actor and event time and are retained without automatic expiry.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}